<p id="p5">But that’s enough of my impressions. I’ll let the developers speak for themselves in this <a href="https://www.macstories.net/podcasts/appstories/" rel="noopener noreferrer">special bonus AppStories video</a>. I came away from New York with some great interviews, which I’ve shared on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@MacStories09" rel="noopener noreferrer">the MacStories YouTube channel</a>. Apologies for the sometimes rough audio. There’s only so much I can do with recordings made in a room packed with press and developers, but if you’re into apps, design, and how things are built, these interviews are for you.</p>
<p id="p6">Also, I left New York with <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-iphone/iphone-duo" rel="noopener noreferrer">a Night Sky 512GB iPhone Duo</a> that I’ve only just set up and begun testing. I’ll be writing about the Duo soon, and we’ll start covering the best of the more than 300 Duo-optimized apps that developers have sent Federico and me. Stay tuned, because the busy fall season at MacStories is just going to keep rolling.</p>
